NNAAMMEE
     aakkbbdd — ADB Keyboard Driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee aaddbb

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aakkbbdd driver provides support for all keyboards attached to the Apple
     Desktop Bus (ADB).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     Devices supported by the aakkbbdd driver include:

     ••   Apple Extended Keyboard
     ••   Apple Keyboard II
     ••   Apple iBook Keyboard
     ••   Apple PowerBook Keyboard

EEVVEENNTTSS
     The aakkbbdd driver sends events to devd(8) for the following events under
     the PPMMUU system:

     ••   Power button - BBuuttttoonn subsystem, pprreesssseedd type.

SSYYSSCCTTLL VVAARRIIAABBLLEESS
     The aakkbbdd driver supports the following sysctl variable for configuring
     the Fn keys:

     _d_e_v_._a_k_b_d_._%_d_._f_n___k_e_y_s___f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n___a_s___p_r_i_m_a_r_y
             Set the Fn keys to be their F-key type as default.  A value of 0
             causes the F-keys keys to work as special keys by default (
             abtn(4)) and a value of 1 sets them to behave as F-keys by de‐
             fault.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     abtn(4), adb(4), cuda(4), pmu(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aakkbbdd device driver appeared in FreeBSD 8.0.

